  notes:"<p class=\"intro-lead\">If you're here, it's because you want to watch the Marvel Cinematic Universe in its most optimized order, a mix of chronological order and release order. You'll find extra details by clicking on each media, and this entire site is guaranteed free of major spoilers.</p><div class=\"intro-tags\"><span class=\"itag\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"/></svg>This guide works for first-time watches as well as rewatches.</span></div><div class=\"keys-title\">How to read this</div><div class=\"keys\"><div class=\"key\"><div class=\"key-h\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><path d=\"M3 12h18M12 3c2.5 3 2.5 15 0 18M12 3c-2.5 3-2.5 15 0 18\"/></svg>The main Earth</div><p>The universe's main chronology takes place on <strong>Earth-616</strong> (sometimes also called Earth-199999). If nothing is specified, it takes place on the main Earth.</p></div><div class=\"key\"><div class=\"key-h\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M11 19 2 12l9-7v14zM22 19l-9-7 9-7v14z\"/></svg>Flashbacks</div><p>Some events work better as a <strong>FLASHBACK</strong> for understanding, and are marked as such.</p></div><div class=\"key\"><div class=\"key-h\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"2\" y=\"4\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M7 20V4M17 20V4M2 9h5M2 15h5M17 9h5M17 15h5\"/></svg>Post-credits scenes</div><p>When watching in chronological order, some post-credits scenes spoil later elements, so I indicate when you should <strong>not</strong> watch them at that point, and also when you should.</p></div><div class=\"key wide\"><div class=\"key-h\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 3l8 3v6c0 5-3.5 8-8 9-4.5-1-8-4-8-9V6l8-3z\"/></svg>Canonicity not confirmed</div><p>Two shows fall under the <strong>\"Canonicity not confirmed\"</strong> category and have therefore never been officially declared part of Earth-616's main timeline by Marvel Studios (Netflix's Defenders shows were no longer canon before becoming canon again). This guide still includes <strong>Agent Carter</strong> and <strong>Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.</strong> (<strong>Cloak &amp; Dagger, Inhumans, The Runaways</strong> are in the same situation but nothing really important happens in them). <strong>Every</strong> existing Marvel audiovisual production is part of the global multiverse anyway, so you can skip them if you want (but they're cool — they add a lot of lore and contradict nothing in the official canon).</p></div></div><details class=\"cuts\"><summary>What's left out, and why<span class=\"n\">10 entries</span><svg class=\"chev\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"cuts-body\"><p class=\"cuts-intro\">Some media is intentionally left out, and the explanations are below:</p><dl class=\"cuts-list\"><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The old Punisher movies</dt><dd>No ties to the rest of the MCU, and the show is way better.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The Blade trilogy and Daredevil/Elektra</dt><dd>Just remember who plays the main characters; beyond that, they add nothing.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The New Mutants</dt><dd>Although part of the X-Men universe, the movie references none of the others and tells its own story.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The X-Men shows</dt><dd>They were never confirmed as canon to the X-Men universe.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The old Fantastic Four movies</dt><dd>Just remember who plays the main characters; beyond that, they add nothing.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>Spider-Noir</dt><dd>The show takes place in its own reality, with no ties to the multiverse whatsoever. But it's really good — watch it after the Spider-Verse movies if you want, to get to know the characters.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>I Am Groot</dt><dd>A string of comedy shorts with no developed story; you can watch only the 1st episode, which bridges Guardians of the Galaxy 1 and 2.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>The SSU (besides Venom)</dt><dd>A universe of mediocre movies with more than questionable connections (even Venom might leave the guide one day).</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>Cartoons with no ties (X-Men '92, X-Men '97, Spider-Man '94, Marvel Rising, M.O.D.O.K, Hit-Monkey, Moon Girl and Devil Dinosaur…)</dt><dd>No ties, but they are part of the Multiverse.</dd></div><div class=\"cut\"><dt>Prelude comics</dt><dd>Canon until a movie contradicts them.</dd></div></dl></div></details>",
